hilippines 2020", "duration_string": "7:07", "is_live": false, "was_live": false, "epoch": 1778003084, "comments": [{"id": "UgwpjRBh7T05Z5w8Vlp4AaABAg", "parent": "root", "text": "pru life policy Holder", "like_count": 1, "author_id": "UCidC1y1oAh0p2Snwxslf36g", "author": "@aileemun5081", "author_thumbnail": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/0gDczgURF8WA-QvAMNNnqX4-3MZKMP50W6fA1Vd_Jg9mU1ATmqoUEhHE1g4cWyw4gJzcPNKx9O4=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "author_is_uploader": false, "author_is_verified": false, "author_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@aileemun5081", "is_favorited": true, "_time_text": "7 months ago", "timestamp": 1759708800, "is_pinned": false}, {"id": "UgwpjRBh7T05Z5w8Vlp4AaABAg.AMnB8i9sGk0AMnCf0c227S", "parent": "UgwpjRBh7T05Z5w8Vlp4AaABAg", "text": "👌 glad to know mam.", "like_count": 0, "author_id": "UCGBySZpSJTjZ632XQ02L6dA", "author": "@PRULancer", "author_thumbnail": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/aPfk_mu-WEhj6UjAVwPfi7cYgAssthWmL74DUSaPeV0wl81c8Y8X895Irp3AqCp5cYnZ_UXr858=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "author_is_uploader": true, "author_is_verified": false, "author_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@PRULancer", "is_favorited": false, "_time_text": "7 months ago", "timestamp": 1759708800, "is_pinned": false}, {"id": "Ugwb5YgoSQWSs0OSaKl4AaABAg", "parent": "root", "text": "Tried gemini with the prompt \"What are the criterias in selecting the best insurance company in the philippines?\" \nBelow is a detailed response that could very well guide us. It did a holistic approach on the subject.\n\nSelecting the best insurance company in the Philippines involves considering several key criteria to ensure you get reliable coverage and service. Here's a comprehensive breakdown:\nI. Financial Stability and Performance:\n * Financial Strength Ratings: Look for companies with strong financial ratings from reputable agencies. The Insurance Commission (IC) in the Philippines monitors and releases performance metrics of insurance companies. Key metrics to consider include:\n   * Premium Income: Total revenue generated from policyholders. A higher premium income generally indicates a larger customer base and market presence.\n   * New Business Annual Premium Equivalent (NBAPE): Measures the value of new policies written, indicating the company's ability to attract new clients and grow.\n   * Net Income: Reflects the company's profitability.\n   * Net Worth: Total assets minus liabilities. A higher net worth signifies a stronger financial foundation and better ability to withstand economic challenges and pay claims.\n   * Total Assets: Demonstrates the company's overall financial strength and its capacity to manage debt repayments.\n   * Solvency Ratio: Indicates the company's ability to meet its long-term financial obligations. A ratio well above the regulatory requirement (e.g., 120% in the Philippines) is a good sign.\n * Company Background and History: Choose a company with a proven track record and a long history of stable operations in the Philippines. This suggests experience and a better understanding of the local market and customer needs.\nII. Products and Coverage:\n * Range of Products: Look for a company that offers a wide range of insurance products (life, health, car, property, investment-linked, etc.) to cater to diverse needs.\n * Specific Policy Features and Benefits:\n   * Coverage Limits: Understand the maximum amount the policy will pay out for different types of claims.\n   * Exclusions and Limitations: Carefully review what is not covered by the policy. This is crucial to avoid surprises during claims.\n   * Riders and Add-ons: Check for optional benefits that can enhance your coverage (e.g., critical illness rider, accidental death benefit).\n   * Cost-effectiveness (Premiums): Compare premiums across different companies for similar coverage. However, don't solely focus on the cheapest option, as it might come with less comprehensive coverage or higher deductibles. Find a balance between affordability and adequate protection.\n   * Deductibles: The amount you have to pay out-of-pocket before the insurance company starts paying.\nIII. Customer Service and Claims Handling:\n * Reputation: Research the company's reputation through online reviews, consumer forums, and feedback from friends and family. Look for companies known for fair practices and customer satisfaction.\n * Claims Handling Process:\n   * Efficiency: How quickly and smoothly does the company process claims?\n   * Responsiveness: Is the company responsive to inquiries and readily available to assist policyholders?\n   * Fairness: Does the company have a reputation for fair claims settlement?\n * Accessibility and Support:\n   * Advisor Support: Does the company provide licensed financial advisors who can help you understand your options and choose the best policy?\n   * Customer Service Channels: Are there multiple ways to contact customer service (phone, email, online chat, physical branches)?\n   * Digital Capabilities: Does the company offer online portals or mobile apps for managing policies, making payments, and filing claims?\nIV. Regulatory Compliance and Trust:\n * Licensed to Operate: Ensure the insurance company is duly licensed by the Insurance Commission (IC) in the Philippines. The IC is the regulatory body that oversees insurance operations and protects policyholders.\n * Transparency: A reputable company will be transparent about its policy terms, conditions, and any potential fees or charges.\n * Adherence to Laws and Regulations: The company should comply with all relevant Philippine insurance laws and regulations, including data privacy laws.\nV. Personal Considerations:\n * Your Specific Needs and Goals: Before looking at companies, assess your own financial situation, dependents, debts, and long-term goals to determine the type and amount of coverage you truly need.\n * Budget: Determine how much you are willing and able to pay in premiums.\n * Your Health Status: For health and life insurance, your health status will impact your premium rates.\n * Trusted Advisor: Consider working with a trusted financial advisor or insurance broker who can provide unbiased advice and help you navigate the options.\nBy carefully evaluating these criteria, you can make an informed decision and select an insurance company in the Philippines that best meets your needs and provides peace of mind.", "like_count": 0, "author_id": "UCuQVnLLyVBfiAiARBmU8XKQ", "author": "@nathanielgargoles7918", "author_thumbnail": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nZhRaL1j_wN7MQCtnN40ytfqQAZpG8scJpYS68MINHn14=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "author_is_uploader": false, "author_is_verified": false, "author_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@nathanielgargoles7918", "is_favorited": false, "_time_text": "11 months ago", "timestamp": 1749168000, "is_pinned": false}, {"id": "UgzurazboO3nQnw9Vxt4AaABAg", "parent": "root", "text": "Cited source discusses Top 10 Life Insurance Companies in the Philippines based on New Business Annual Premium Equivalent ONLY\n\nNBAPE is just one of the many factors worth considering. You may want to try searching with the help of google gemini (AI) that provides reliable sources for verification.", "like_count": 0, "author_id": "UCuQVnLLyVBfiAiARBmU8XKQ", "author": "@nathanielgargoles7918", "author_thumbnail": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nZhRaL1j_wN7MQCtnN40ytfqQAZpG8scJpYS68MINHn14=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "author_is_uploader": false, "author_is_verified": false, "author_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@nathanielgargoles7918", "is_favorited": false, "_time_text": "11 months ago", "timestamp": 1749168000, "is_pinned": false}, {"id": "Ugy3LjI9Cd0xaJ_sP_R4AaABAg", "parent": "root", "text": "Proud sunlife policy holder..two policy😅2,500/1100..nice to heard number 2 ang sunlife", "like_count": 1, "author_id": "UCmdY8l_TvRntNl2aUgnTHYQ", "author": "@raradomingo4452", "author_thumbnail": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_lp9OQ-_ykMGuXZ9KrcKyPSm9kA9vB9cMF5T5UXie-0OmMMmgygTjG1BuATiGxiSrkuCQ=s88-c-k-